{"type":"message","id":"1abb6882","parentId":"ff0a6b24","timestamp":"2026-06-15T07:10:17.723Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, I don't see any \"开仓\" events after 14:49. But the log from verify_trades.py showed the ETH short failure. The positions went from 4 to 5. Let me check more broadly - maybe there was an additional position re-opening or a SOL trade happening.\n\nWait, I actually checked more carefully. The SOL position IS back with the same entry price $70.92. That's the same entry as before. So it seems like either:\n1. The close didn't actually happen (maybe it didn't fully close), or\n2. The monitor re-opened it\n\nLet me check the SOL close log again. The close showed \"✅ 平仓成功\", so it should have been closed. But then it's back with the same entry price...\n\nWait, looking at the output from query_positions.py more carefully - the SOL entry is at $70.92, which is the same as before. The close I did was at $71.39... Hmm, but the system shows 5 positions now, including SOL.\n\nMaybe the monitor's local cache wasn't updated when I closed SOL externally, and it still thinks SOL is there. Then when the monitor tried to open BTC, it saw 5 positions and skipped.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. I closed SOL via manual_trade.py. The monitor runs independently. The monitor checks positions via the Binance API every ~90 seconds. So after I close SOL, the monitor's next position check should see 4 positions.\n\nBut the log at 14:52:31 shows API 持仓=5. So the Binance API is returning 5 positions. This means the SOL position didn't actually get closed, or a new position was opened immediately after.\n\nWait, the close output said \"orderId=2217882456 status=NEW\" - then it said \"✅ 平仓成功\". But the entry price $70.92 and current price $70.17 match the old position... \n\nLet me check if the close really executed. Maybe the order went to \"NEW\" but then got filled. The script checks after submitting - let me look at the close output again:\n\n```\n2026-06-15 14:49:05 [INFO] ✅ 订单确认 orderId=2217882456 status=NEW\n2026-06-15 14:49:10 [INFO] 🗑️ SOLUSDT Algo 单已取消 algoId=1000000106760819\n2026-06-15 14:49:12 [INFO] 🗑️ SOLUSDT Algo 单已取消 algoId=1000000106760799\n✅ 平仓成功\n```\n\nHmm, \"status=NEW\" - that means the order was placed but may not have been filled immediately. The script says \"✅ 平仓成功\" but maybe it actually didn't fill. The SOL position with entry $70.92 is still there.\n\nThe SOL position entry price ($70.92) is EXACTLY the same as before I closed it. This is very suspicious. It's the exact same position.\n\nMy theory: the close order was submitted as NEW but never got filled, or was cancelled/expired. The position remained open. And then the monitor's position count stayed at 5.\n\nActually, looking at the manual_trade.py output more carefully, it says orderId=2217882456 and status=NEW, then later \"✅ 平仓成功\" and \"✅ SOL 残余 SL/TP 挂单已清理\". The script considers the trade done but the API is still showing the position.\n\nThis might be an issue with the manual_trade.py script - it submitted the close order but didn't properly wait for it to fill before declaring success. Or the order got filled but then got reversed.\n\nLet me look at the Binance trade history to confirm what happened.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_rvFpZhGn7B2kkWhf6T2E6006","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -E '14:49|14:50|14:51' /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log | head -30","timeout":8}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":818,"output":1720,"cacheRead":36224,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":38762,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781507399693}}
