{"type":"message","id":"afb901be","parentId":"c380b76e","timestamp":"2026-06-15T07:10:30.768Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the key finding: at 14:49:02 (just 4 seconds after I closed SOL), the monitor's position check already showed 5 positions. The SOL position was never actually removed from the Binance API - the close order status was \"NEW\" meaning it was placed but not filled.\n\nLet me look more carefully:\n- 14:49:02 - Already 5 positions (right after my close at ~14:49:00)\n- 14:50:43 - Still 5 positions\n\nThis confirms the SOL position was never actually closed. The order was placed (status=NEW) but never filled.\n\nSo the problem is that SOL didn't actually get closed. The manual_trade.py script declared success but the order likely expired or was rejected.\n\nI should try closing it again, maybe with a different approach. But first let me tell the husband what happened and try closing it again. \n\nActually, wait - the close order was placed at 14:49:05 with orderId=2217882456, status=NEW. But looking at the log, at 14:49:02 the monitor reports 5 positions. So the close was submitted at 14:49:05 and at 14:50:43 it's still 5 positions. Maybe the market order didn't fill.\n\nLet me try to close SOL again, this time more carefully.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] SOL 的平仓单其实没成交——下单状态是 NEW 但没撮合成功，脚本误报\"成功\"了。14:49 设的平仓单没执行，SOL 还在。我再平一次。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_oJhanDwQbd9HmPIgzGLY5233","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace && python3 scripts/manual_trade.py close SOL --confirm 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":504,"output":706,"cacheRead":39808,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":41018,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781507421865}}
