{"type":"message","id":"fd2ff55e","parentId":"65398c68","timestamp":"2026-06-15T07:10:45.902Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now it's rejecting with `-2022 ReduceOnly Order is rejected`. This is a Binance-specific error. Looking at it more carefully: the quantity is 2.38, but the position was 2.82 last time. So the remaining position is now 2.38 instead of 2.82? Or maybe the first close partially filled?\n\nWait, the first close was for 2.82 @ $71.39. Now it's trying to close 2.38. So maybe 0.44 was actually filled? But the position is still there with entry $70.92.\n\nThe `-2022 ReduceOnly Order is rejected` error happens when a reduce-only order would increase the position. This means the position might have been reduce-only and the system is confused about the current position state. \n\nThis looks like the earlier close might have partially succeeded but left the position in a weird state, and now trying to close again gets rejected.\n\nLet me try a different approach - maybe close the position without the reduce-only flag, or check if there are open orders that need to be cancelled first.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"SOL 平仓被币安拒了 `-2022 ReduceOnly rejected`，看起来第一次平仓可能部分成交导致仓位状态异常。让我换个方式处理。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_E80YrlkZY68DSugHpKMa7116","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace && python3 scripts/manual_trade.py cancel SOL 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":466,"output":571,"cacheRead":40704,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":41741,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781507437341}}
