{"type":"message","id":"51e76c3d","parentId":"c539ef6b","timestamp":"2026-06-15T07:11:00.183Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, cancelled all open orders for SOL. Now the question is: is the position actually still open or not? Let me check the current state. The quantity was 2.38, which is less than the original 2.82 - maybe the first close partially filled. But query_positions still shows the position.\n\nActually, I think the error `-2022 ReduceOnly Order is rejected` could also mean the position might already be closed but the query is showing stale data. Or the position has a reduce-only restriction.\n\nLet me try a different angle - maybe use the `close-all` command or try to close it through a regular market sell order instead of reduce-only.\n\nBut wait, manual_trade.py uses reduce-only for closing. Let me check if there's a way to do a regular sell. Or maybe I should check if the position actually exists by looking at open orders.\n\nLet me also check the binance_auto_trade.py script to see if there's a close function there.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_W99JnCJWyJBesN9i8aAi7637","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace && python3 -c \"\nfrom scripts.binance_auto_trade import AutoTrader\ntrader = AutoTrader()\n# Check open orders for SOL\norders = trader.get_open_orders('SOLUSDT')\nprint(f'SOL 挂单数: {len(orders) if orders else 0}')\nfor o in (orders or []):\n    print(f'  {o}')\n# Check specific position\npos = trader.get_position('SOLUSDT')\nif pos:\n    print(f'SOL仓位: 数量={pos.get(\\\"positionAmt\\\")}, 入场={pos.get(\\\"entryPrice\\\")}, 未实现盈亏={pos.get(\\\"unRealizedProfit\\\")}')\nelse:\n    print('SOL仓位: 无')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":276,"output":640,"cacheRead":41472,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":42388,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":