{"type":"message","id":"332d42ab","parentId":"5e5333cd","timestamp":"2026-06-15T07:12:15.832Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me think about this more carefully. The ReduceOnly error on SOL means the system might think the position doesn't exist or something weird is going on. Let me try to close it via a different method - maybe by placing a regular MARKET SELL order (without reduce_only). \n\nActually wait, looking back at the output from the second close attempt:\n```\n数量: 2.38 (was 2.82 in first attempt)\n```\n\nSo the first close attempt at 14:49 might have partially filled - 0.44 was filled, leaving 2.38. But the position still shows up in the query with entry $70.92.\n\nThe -2022 error could be because there's something wrong with the reduce_only flag or the position is in a state where reduce_only doesn't work.\n\nLet me try a different approach: use binance_auto_trade to close the position via the close_position method which might handle it differently.\n\nOr maybe I should just try to place a regular market sell with the exact quantity of the remaining position.\n\nLet me try using the API directly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_IFBSyPXclSTK3Alh6u9I2281","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace && python3 -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0, 'scripts')\nimport json, hmac, hashlib, time, requests, urllib3\nurllib3.disable_warnings()\n\n# Load config\nfrom manual_trade import load_config\ncfg = load_config()\napi_key, api_secret = cfg['api_key'], cfg['api_secret']\nbase = 'https://testnet.binancefuture.com'\nproxies = {'https': 'http://127.0.0.1:7890'}\n\n# 1. Get SOL position info\nts = int(time.time() * 1000)\nqs = f'timestamp={ts}'\nsig = hmac.new(api_secret.encode(), qs.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\nr = requests.get(f'{base}/fapi/v2/positionRisk?symbol=SOLUSDT&{qs}&signature={sig}',\n    headers={'X-MBX-APIKEY': api_key}, proxies=proxies, verify=False)\npos_data = r.json()\nfor p in pos_data:\n    amt = float(p['positionAmt'])\n    ep = float(p['entryPrice'])\n    print(f'SOL: positionAmt={amt}, entryPrice={ep}, unrealizedPnL={p[\\\"unRealizedProfit\\\"]}')\n\n# 2. Try to close with MARKET order, quantity=abs(amt), side=SELL if amt>0 else BUY\nif amt != 0:\n    qty = abs(amt)\n    side = 'SELL' if amt > 0 else 'BUY'\n    \n    ts2 = int(time.time() * 1000)\n    params = f'symbol=SOLUSDT&side={side}&type=MARKET&quantity={qty}&reduceOnly=true&timestamp={ts2}'\n    sig2 = hmac.new(api_secret.encode(), params.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n    \n    r2 = requests.post(f'{base}/fapi/v1/order?{params}&signature={sig2}',\n        headers={'X-MBX-APIKEY': api_key}, proxies=proxies, verify=False)\n    result = r2.json()\n    print(f'Close result: {json.dumps(result, indent=2)}')\nelse:\n    print('No position to close')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":105,"output":1028,"cacheRead":45184,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":46317,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781507520661}}
