{"type":"message","id":"fed30b70","parentId":"848f85e9","timestamp":"2026-06-15T07:13:04.063Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now this is very interesting! `bat.get_all_positions()` returns only 3 positions:\n- BNB LONG\n- XRP LONG  \n- LINK SHORT\n\nBut query_positions.py shows 5 positions including SOL LONG and ETH SHORT. This means query_positions.py is supplementing from `crypto_positions.json` (local cache) when the real API returns fewer positions.\n\nSo the actual Binance state is:\n- BNB LONG\n- XRP LONG\n- LINK SHORT\n\nThe SOL and ETH positions in query_positions.py are coming from the local cache file `crypto_positions.json`, not from the real API!\n\nThis means:\n1. SOL was actually closed (partially at 14:49, showing 0.44 filled)\n2. ETH might have also been closed or expired\n3. The real position count is only 3, well under the 4 limit\n4. But the local cache still shows 5, causing the monitor to think it's at max capacity\n\nThis is a stale cache issue! The `crypto_positions.json` file has stale data that doesn't match the actual API. That's why:\n- Monitor thinks there are 5 positions (from cache + API merge)\n- Actually there are only 3 positions on Binance\n- New signals are being blocked by the stale cache count\n\nSo the solution isn't to close more positions - it's to fix the stale cache. Let me check the crypto_positions.json and possibly clear it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"找到根因了！不是币安的问题。\n\n**实际 Binance API 现在只有 3 个持仓：BNB、XRP、LINK**。但 `crypto_positions.json` 本地缓存还有 5 条旧数据（SOL 和 ETH），monitor 被过期缓存骗了，一直在自我拦截。\n\nSOL 其实已经平掉了，ETH 大概也是类似情况。让我清理缓存。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_de09lVVBah89LQovCH8m0684","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_positions.json | python3 -m json.tool 2>&1 | head -40","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":362,"output":800,"cach