{"type":"message","id":"1cca788b","parentId":"c9accdf1","timestamp":"2026-06-15T16:07:42.500Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"BNB SHORT entry around 633 was probably opened around 21:23 when the previous BNB LONG was closed at TP. Let me check more thoroughly.\n\nBNB was closed at TP1 at 21:23:55. A new BNB SHORT was opened. Let me find when.\n\nLINK LONG was opened at 21:19.\n\nNow let me think about why BNB and LINK SL/TP aren't being actively updated in recent logs:\n\nFor BNB SHORT (entry 633, SL 645.7, current 628.3):\n- The SL is far above (645.7 vs entry 633), and the current price is BELOW entry (628.3) which is good for a SHORT\n- For a short position, trailing SL moves DOWN as price goes down\n- The SL might be the initial SL and hasn't been trailed yet because price hasn't moved enough\n\nFor LINK LONG (entry 8.453, SL 8.284, current 8.53):\n- The SL is below entry and current price is slightly above entry\n- SL hasn't been trailed yet because price hasn't moved enough upward\n\nSo the answer is: SOL and XRP had active trailing because their prices were moving significantly. BNB and LINK are newer positions with less dramatic price movement - their SL hasn't triggered trailing updates yet, or the trailing updates are less frequent.\n\nActually wait, BNB SHORT and LINK LONG are relatively new. Let me check when BNB SHORT was opened.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_w2231Gri2bI1pfpAPJdJ4290","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -E '开空 BNB|开空.*BNB' /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log | grep '2026-06-15' | tail -3","timeout":8}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":149,"output":731,"cacheRead":79232,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":80112,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781539654212}}
